msgctxt "180"
msgid ""
"What's wrong, Izumi? You're usually the first one at the\r\n"
"dinner table."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "192"
msgid "...I don't wanna eat right now."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "204"
msgid "What? Are you feeling okay?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "216"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "228"
msgid "(Something's definitely bothering her...)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "240"
msgid "Not hungry, huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "252"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "264"
msgid "Does your stomach hurt?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "276"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "288"
msgid "Izumi?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "300"
msgid "No, I feel fine..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "312"
msgid "(Guess that wasn't it. Maybe...)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "324"
msgid "Did something happen at school?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "336"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "348"
msgid "Come on, Izumi. You can tell me."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "360"
msgid "...Hey, Uncle Kaz?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "372"
msgid "What's up?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "384"
msgid "Is not having parents... a bad thing?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "396"
msgid "Huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "408"
msgid ""
"The other kids at school were making fun of me 'cause\r\n"
"I don't have a mom and dad."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "420"
msgid "How'd that even get brought up?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "432"
msgid ""
"Well, Bring Your Parents to School Day is pretty soon,\r\n"
"so everyone started asking what I was gonna do."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "444"
msgid "Uh-huh..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "456"
msgid "They... They said my parents can't come 'cause they're dead."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "468"
msgid "(That's awful...)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "480"
msgid "Everyone knows I live here with you, Uncle Kaz."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "492"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "504"
msgid ""
"And it's not like I want you to pretend to be my dad or\r\n"
"anything, but..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "516"
msgid "But what, Izumi? You can tell me."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "528"
msgid "It's... really hard."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "540"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "552"
msgid ""
"Like, some of the other parents can't come 'cause they're\r\n"
"too busy, but nobody makes fun of those kids. Why not!?\r\n"
"Why can't I just have a real family like everyone else!?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "564"
msgid "Let's talk about this after dinner, okay?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "576"
msgid "Just go if you're hungry! I wanna stay here."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "588"
msgid ""
"Come on, you're not gonna grow big and strong if you don't\r\n"
"eat your dinner."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "600"
msgid "You can't tell me what to do! You're not my dad!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "612"
msgid "Izumi!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "624"
msgid ""
"Just leave me alone! I don't have a family, so I can do\r\n"
"what I want!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "636"
msgid "You're wrong."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "648"
msgid "You do have a family, Izumi."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "660"
msgid "Huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "672"
msgid "Me, Haruka, and everyone else."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "684"
msgid "I don't get it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "696"
msgid ""
"Listen. Families come in all shapes and sizes. Having a \"real\" mom and "
"dad isn't what matters here."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "708"
msgid "But..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "720"
msgid ""
"What matters is that you're surrounded by people who love\r\n"
"you for who you are."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "732"
msgid "But we're not related."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "744"
msgid "Well, there's more to it than that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "756"
msgid ""
"Related or not, you mean the world to all of us. That alone\r\n"
"is enough to make us family."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "768"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "780"
msgid ""
"And besides, I don't think your classmates were really\r\n"
"making fun of you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "792"
msgid "Huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "804"
msgid ""
"They've spent their whole lives with their moms and dads\r\n"
"right by their side. They can't imagine it any other way."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "816"
msgid ""
"I'm sure they just don't realize how lonely life as an\r\n"
"orphan can be."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "828"
msgid "Then... they don't think I'm weird?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "840"
msgid ""
"That's right. If anything, I'd say they were genuinely\r\n"
"concerned about you feeling lonely."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "852"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "864"
msgid "I was an orphan, too. I know just how hard it can be."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "876"
msgid ""
"Even so, I'll always think of the man who brought me up\r\n"
"as my real dad."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "888"
msgid "And the other kids from my orphanage? They're my siblings."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "900"
msgid ""
"Throughout all my time there... the idea of not having\r\n"
"a real family never even crossed my mind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "912"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "924"
msgid ""
"So you see? You have everything you could ever need right\r\n"
"here at Morning Glory."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "936"
msgid ""
"Your family's just as real as any of the other kids' at\r\n"
"school. You don't need to be jealous of them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "948"
msgid "I'm not! It's just, they say things sometimes..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "960"
msgid "And when they do, you can tell them this."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "972"
msgid "\"I'm not alone. I have nine people in my family.\""
msgstr ""

msgctxt "984"
msgid "Nine?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "996"
msgid "Me, Haruka, and the others. That makes nine."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1008"
msgid "We're... a family, huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1032"
msgid "Not hungry, huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1044"
msgid "Something happen at school?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1056"
msgid "Let's talk about this after dinner."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1068"
msgid "You do have one, Izumi."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "10088"
msgid "Kiryu"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "10092"
msgid "Izumi"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "10096"
msgid "P_sitgrd_tlk_jibeta_yes"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "10100"
msgid "P_sitgrd_tlk_jibeta_no"
msgstr ""